# First Alliance horse from Katie Hunter (Eastvale Logging Camp).
# Sources: Forever client 1.60.1.70338 tables via wago.tools (ItemSparse: level,
# price, races, riding spell; SkillLineAbility: Riding); npcs.json and
# items.json for the trainer, the vendor and its stock.
# Forever riding: the client files every racial riding spell under one Riding
# skill (SkillLineAbility), so any riding trainer of your faction teaches it:
# Apprentice Riding (skill 75) from level 40, Journeyman Riding (150) at 60.
# Blizzard: learning to ride grants a mount, and training costs 100g at 40 and
# 1,000g at 60 (Kris Zierhut). ItemSparse lists the
# mounts at 20g (level 40) and 200g (level 60), usable by every race of the
# faction; whether a vendor still wants Exalted with another race's city (the
# Era rule) is server-side and unconfirmed.

step Learn to ride
  zone Elwynn Forest
  tip Randal Hunter and Katie Hunter's horse pen are at Eastvale Logging Camp in eastern Elwynn Forest. At 40 Randal Hunter teaches Riding (100g per Blizzard's designers), and learning it gives you a mount. The Forever client lets every Alliance race ride these.
  level 40
  train 4732                          -- Randal Hunter, riding trainer
  skill Riding 75

step Pick a colour
  tip Katie Hunter sells the other colours (20g each in the Forever client). Buy any you want, or none if the mount you were given is the one you like.
  vendor 384                          -- Katie Hunter
  buy 2414 npc 384 optional           -- Pinto Bridle, 20g
  buy 5655 npc 384 optional           -- Chestnut Mare Bridle, 20g
  buy 5656 npc 384 optional           -- Brown Horse Bridle, 20g
  note Black Stallion Bridle is in the client, but no vendor is confirmed to sell it in Forever.
